# Local production verification only - fronts the natively-running uvicorn
# web service on one primary URL (http://localhost:8080) the way a real
# reverse proxy would, so what you browse-test locally matches the deployed
# shape. Plain HTTP on purpose: a locally-trusted cert is not the same thing
# as a publicly trusted one, and pretending otherwise here would be
# misleading. Security headers (CSP/HSTS/X-Frame-Options/etc) are already
# set by the app itself (app/main.py's security_headers middleware, with
# HSTS correctly gated on request.url.scheme=="https") - not duplicated
# here. See deploy/Caddyfile for the public/Docker production config (real
# HTTPS via DOMAIN - a genuinely different tier, not a duplicate).
http://localhost:8080 {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8010
	header -Server
}
